# ============================================================
# horse_race.R — model comparison for the turbulence composite
#
# QUESTION (PJ, 16 Aug): the break/Chow apparatus assumes the series takes a
# STEPPED form. Does the data prefer a step, or a smooth rise? Decide it on a
# criterion rather than on argument.
#
# FIVE MODELS, same response, same n, same estimator family:
#   M0 flat        y = a                                    k = 2
#   M1 linear      y = a + b t                              k = 3
#   M2 quadratic   y = a + b t + c t^2                      k = 4
#   M3 break       y = a1 + b1 t (t<=K); a2 + b2 t (t>K)    k = 6   (K searched)
#   M4 segmented   y = a + b1 t + b2 (t-C)+                 k = 5   (C searched)
#   M5 spline      y = a + s(t), thin-plate, mgcv           k = edf + 1
#
# k counts EVERY estimated quantity including sigma and the searched break
# date / knot. BIC = n*log(RSS/n) + k*log(n), computed identically for all five
# so the numbers are comparable.
#
# FOUR CRITERIA, because no single one settles it:
#   (a) AIC          — lenient, favours flexibility
#   (b) BIC          — the criterion PJ asked for
#   (c) LOO-CV RMSE  — the break date / knot is RE-SEARCHED INSIDE EACH FOLD, so
#                      the break model is charged honestly for its search. This
#                      is the criterion that does not depend on a parameter-
#                      counting convention, and is the tie-breaker.
#   (d) AR(1)-error BIC — annual series are autocorrelated; the whole
#                      break-vs-trend literature (Perron vs its critics) turns
#                      on whether the "break" is serial correlation in disguise.
#
# The break model follows chow_standardized/chow_test.R exactly: level+trend
# split (p = 2), 15% interior trim, min 3 obs per segment.
#
# Also runs the same race on each of the six COMPONENT z-series, to test
# whether any verdict is general or specific to the composite.
#
# Reads : composite_canonical/canonical_pc1_1979_2025.csv  (clean six, 18 Aug; window now 1979-2025 -
#         the FILENAME is a legacy misnomer and is deliberately left alone until the whole
#         chapter is renamed, so that references do not break mid-lockdown)
# Writes: nonlinear_modelling/{horse_race_composite,horse_race_components,
#         fit_predictions}.csv, fig_horse_race.png, run.log
# NO API SPEND. Seed 42.
# ============================================================

